verses.text:
“Deserving are you, our Lord and our God,
of taking the glory, the honor, and the power;
for you made all things,
and it is by your desire that they existed and were created.”{f}

For this reason they are before God’s throne
and serve him by day and by night in his sanctuary;
the one seated on the throne will spread a shelter over them.{h}

Never again will they be hungry, never again thirsty;
no sun will beat down on them,
no burning heat,{i}

for the Lamb who is at the throne’s center will be their shepherd;
he will guide them to fountains of life-giving water,
and every tear God will wipe from their eyes.”{j}

Then a loud voice in heaven said,
“Salvation and strength have come at last,
along with the kingdom of our God
and the authority of his Christ;
for the prosecutor of our brothers and sisters,
who charged them before our God both day and night,
has been hurled down.{f}

Whoever is meant for captivity
will go to captivity;
whoever kills by the sword
must be killed by the sword.
Here is the call for the endurance and faithfulness of God’s holy people.{i}

And I heard the angel who presides over the waters declaring,
“You are righteous—who are and who were, the Holy One—
because you have rendered this verdict;{c}

they shed the blood of the holy and of the prophets,
and blood you have given them to drink;
they have earned it!”

And I heard the altar answer,
“Yes, O Lord God, the Almighty,
your verdicts are true and righteous!”{d}

Give back to her what she has given,
and pay her twice over according to her deeds;
in the cup that she mixed for others, mix twice as much for her.{f}

Give her pain and mourning
to match the glory she gave herself and her wanton luxury.
In her heart she boasts,
‘Enthroned as a queen I sit;
widow I am not,
and mourning I shall never know.’{g}

Rejoice over her, O heaven,
you holy people, apostles, and prophets,
because God has pronounced your sentence on her!”{r}

No more will the music of harp and song,
of pipe and trumpet,
be heard within you;
never again will any craftsman of any trade
be found within you;
never again will the grinding of the mill
be heard within you;{t}

No lamp will ever again give light in you;
never again will the voices of a bridegroom and a bride sound within you.
Your merchants were the world’s great men,
and by your sorcery all the nations were led astray.{u}

After this I heard what seemed a great noise, the voice of an immense multitude in heaven, saying,
“Hallelujah!
Salvation and glory and power are our God’s,{a}

And a second time they cried out,
“Hallelujah!
Her smoke rises for ever and ever.”{c}

Let us rejoice and exult,
and let us give the glory to him,
for the marriage of the Lamb has arrived,
and his bride has prepared herself.{g}

Every tear will be wiped by him from their eyes.
Death will be no more;
no more mourning, no more crying, no more suffering,
for the former things have gone.”{d}
